P1-1 — FAIL review tracking is still not reconciled to the failing lane or to itemized register entries.
scripts/check_smp1_contract.py:270-281 recomputes one global total across protocol.p1_open/p2_open/p3_open for every failing review lane. Any non-empty entry for any other lane therefore marks every FAIL lane as tracked, even when the failing lane has no itemized finding and no same-lane PASS. The code also applies len() without requiring arrays of item strings and does not inspect the derived finding register. This contradicts SMP1 section 10's per-review requirement that review rounds be same-lane-PASS-superseded or itemized as open findings in both the machine summary and finding register. Commit a4f9fb9 closes the exact all-empty/no-PASS case, but not the underlying silent-pending bypass identified in rereview 2.

